<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: Czech Zivnostenska H1 net profit drops.</title>
<headline>Czech Zivnostenska H1 net profit drops.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Prague-based Zivnostenska Banka a.s. said on Tuesday that its first-half after-tax profit fell to 166 million crowns from 268 million crowns for the same period last year, according to Czech accounting standards.  </p>
<p>(in millions of crowns)</p>
<p> after-tax profit	    166.376	  267.742</p>
<p> depreciation		    N/A	     78.297</p>
<p> basic capital	     1,360.410	1,360.410</p>
<p> liabilities to banks   14,180.955     11,869.851</p>
<p> liabilities to clients 18,430.514     16,551.906</p>
<p> debt securities in issue    0.000	1,000.000</p>
<p> loans to banks		889.760	1,480.377</p>
<p> loans to clients	 11,220.525     10,019.304</p>
<p> balance sheet total    36,336.401     33,266.132</p>
<p>Note: According to the latest Central Securities Registry report earlier this month, Zivnostenska Banka's largest shareholders were Germany's BHF-Bank AG with a 47 percent stake, and the International Finance Corporation with a 10 percent stake.</p>
<p>-- Prague Newsroom, 420-2-2423-0003</p>
